---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { loadContent } from "../../lib/content";
import { calBookingUrl } from "../../lib/site";

const { provider } = loadContent();
---

<Layout
  title={`Quadratic Equations | CBSE Class 10 Maths | ${provider.name}`}
  description="Comprehensive CBSE Class 10 Maths Chapter 4 study notes on Quadratic Equations. Standard form, factorization method, quadratic formula (Sridharacharya), nature of roots (discriminant D), word problems, and an interactive 20-question board quiz."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <nav class="small" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/subjects/">Subjects</a> / <a href="/resources/">Resources</a> / Quadratic Equations
    </nav>

    <div class="resource-header">
      <span class="eyebrow">CBSE Class 10 · Mathematics · Chapter 4</span>
      <h1>Quadratic Equations</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Master quadratic factorisation, the quadratic formula, discriminant conditions for the nature of roots, and high-frequency board word problems (speed, age, geometry).
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Concepts -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Key Concepts &amp; Formulas</h2>

      <div class="grid two concept-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>📐 Standard Form of a Quadratic Equation</h3>
          <p class="formula">ax² + bx + c = 0, &nbsp;(a ≠ 0)</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>Where <em>a, b, c</em> are real numbers and <em>a ≠ 0</em>.</li>
            <li>If <em>a = 0</em>, the equation degenerates into a linear equation (<em>bx + c = 0</em>).</li>
            <li>A quadratic equation has <strong>at most two real roots</strong>.</li>
            <li>A real number <em>α</em> is called a root/solution of <em>ax² + bx + c = 0</em> if <code>aα² + bα + c = 0</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>⚡ Solving by Factorisation (Middle Term Splitting)</h3>
          <p class="formula">ax² + bx + c = a(x - α)(x - β) = 0</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>Find two numbers <em>p</em> and <em>q</em> such that:
              <br/><code>p + q = b</code> &nbsp;and&nbsp; <code>p · q = a · c</code>.
            </li>
            <li>Split the middle term: <code>ax² + px + qx + c = 0</code>.</li>
            <li>Group terms and factor out common binomials to find roots: <code>x = α</code> or <code>x = β</code>.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>🔍 Quadratic Formula (Sridharacharya's Rule)</h3>
          <p class="formula">x = [-b ± √(b² - 4ac)] / (2a)</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li>The quantity <code>D = b² - 4ac</code> is called the <strong>Discriminant</strong>.</li>
            <li>If <em>D ≥ 0</em>, real roots exist:
              <br/><code>α = (-b + √D) / (2a)</code>, &nbsp; <code>β = (-b - √D) / (2a)</code>.
            </li>
            <li>If <em>D &lt; 0</em>, no real roots exist.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>⚖️ Nature of Roots Flowchart</h3>
          <p class="formula">D = b² - 4ac governs root behavior</p>
          <ul class="clean-list">
            <li><strong>Case 1: D &gt; 0</strong> ⟹ Two distinct (unequal) real roots.</li>
            <li><strong>Case 2: D = 0</strong> ⟹ Two equal (coincident/repeated) real roots: <code>x = -b / (2a)</code>.</li>
            <li><strong>Case 3: D &lt; 0</strong> ⟹ No real roots (roots are complex/imaginary).</li>
            <li><em>Rational roots condition:</em> If <em>a, b, c</em> are rational and <em>D</em> is a perfect square (&gt; 0), roots are rational and distinct.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Visual Diagrams Section -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Visual Concepts: Discriminant Decision Tree &amp; Parabola Roots</h2>

      <div class="grid two">
        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 1 · Nature of Roots Decision Tree</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Discriminant nature of roots tree">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- Root Box: D = b² - 4ac -->
              <rect x="150" y="20" width="160" height="35" rx="6" fill="#0f766e"/>
              <text x="230" y="42" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">D = b² - 4ac</text>

              <!-- Branch lines -->
              <line x1="180" y1="55" x2="80" y2="100" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="2"/>
              <line x1="230" y1="55" x2="230" y2="100" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="2"/>
              <line x1="280" y1="55" x2="380" y2="100" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="2"/>

              <!-- Left Node: D > 0 -->
              <g transform="translate(15, 100)">
                <rect x="0" y="0" width="130" height="120" rx="6" fill="#ecfdf5" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <text x="65" y="25" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#065f46">D &gt; 0</text>
                <text x="65" y="45" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#047857">Two Distinct</text>
                <text x="65" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#047857">Real Roots</text>
                <line x1="15" y1="75" x2="115" y2="75" stroke="#a7f3d0" stroke-width="1"/>
                <text x="65" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#065f46">x = (-b ± √D)/2a</text>
                <text x="65" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#059669">2 X-intercepts</text>
              </g>

              <!-- Center Node: D = 0 -->
              <g transform="translate(165, 100)">
                <rect x="0" y="0" width="130" height="120" rx="6" fill="#fef3c7" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <text x="65" y="25" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#92400e">D = 0</text>
                <text x="65" y="45" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#b45309">Two Equal</text>
                <text x="65" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#b45309">Real Roots</text>
                <line x1="15" y1="75" x2="115" y2="75" stroke="#fde68a" stroke-width="1"/>
                <text x="65" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#92400e">x = -b / (2a)</text>
                <text x="65" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#b45309">Touches X-axis</text>
              </g>

              <!-- Right Node: D < 0 -->
              <g transform="translate(315, 100)">
                <rect x="0" y="0" width="130" height="120" rx="6" fill="#fee2e2" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="1.5"/>
                <text x="65" y="25" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12" font-weight="700" fill="#991b1b">D &lt; 0</text>
                <text x="65" y="45" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#b91c1c">No Real Roots</text>
                <text x="65" y="60" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#b91c1c">(Imaginary)</text>
                <line x1="15" y1="75" x2="115" y2="75" stroke="#fecaca" stroke-width="1"/>
                <text x="65" y="95" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#991b1b">√(-negative) ∉ ℝ</text>
                <text x="65" y="110" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="#b91c1c">No X-intercept</text>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">Discriminant D determines whether roots are distinct real, repeated real, or non-real.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card visual-card">
          <div class="visual-badge">Visual Diagram 2 · Train Speed &amp; Time Word Problem Blueprint</div>
          <div class="svg-container">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 460 250" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Train speed time problem model">
              <rect width="460" height="250" fill="#f8fafc" rx="8"/>
              
              <!-- Track -->
              <line x1="30" y1="110" x2="430" y2="110" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="3"/>
              <line x1="30" y1="120" x2="430" y2="120" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="3"/>
              <!-- Ties -->
              <line x1="70" y1="105" x2="70" y2="125" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
              <line x1="140" y1="105" x2="140" y2="125" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
              <line x1="210" y1="105" x2="210" y2="125" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
              <line x1="280" y1="105" x2="280" y2="125" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>
              <line x1="350" y1="105" x2="350" y2="125" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/>

              <!-- Distance Marker -->
              <rect x="180" y="60" width="100" height="24" rx="4" fill="#0284c7"/>
              <text x="230" y="76" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#fff">Distance = d km</text>

              <!-- Normal Speed Train -->
              <rect x="40" y="145" width="170" height="75" rx="6" fill="#f1f5f9" stroke="#0284c7" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <text x="125" y="165" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#0369a1">Usual Speed: x km/h</text>
              <text x="125" y="185" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#0f172a">Time t₁ = d / x</text>
              <text x="125" y="205" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" fill="#64748b">Takes longer time</text>

              <!-- Increased Speed Train -->
              <rect x="250" y="145" width="170" height="75" rx="6" fill="#f1f5f9" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="1.5"/>
              <text x="335" y="165" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" font-weight="700" fill="#047857">Increased: (x + 5) km/h</text>
              <text x="335" y="185" text-anchor="middle" font-size="11" fill="#0f172a">Time t₂ = d / (x + 5)</text>
              <text x="335" y="205" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="#059669">Difference: t₁ - t₂ = Δt</text>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <p class="visual-caption">Standard board exam algebraic formulation: d/x - d/(x + Δx) = time difference.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Solved Step-by-Step Problem -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Exemplar Board Problem: Quadratic Speed Word Problem Solved</h2>
      <div class="card" style="padding:1.75rem; background:var(--paper)">
        <h3 style="color:var(--brand);margin-top:0">Problem: An express train takes 1 hour less than a passenger train to travel 132 km between Mysore and Bangalore. If the average speed of the express train is 11 km/h more than that of the passenger train, find the average speed of the two trains.</h3>
        <div style="font-size:0.95rem; line-height:1.7; color:var(--text)">
          <p><strong>Step 1 (Assume variables):</strong> Let the average speed of the passenger train be <em>x km/h</em>.
            <br/>Then average speed of the express train = <code>(x + 11) km/h</code>.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 2 (Express time taken):</strong>
            <br/>Time taken by passenger train: <code>t₁ = 132 / x hours</code>
            <br/>Time taken by express train: <code>t₂ = 132 / (x + 11) hours</code>
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 3 (Formulate quadratic equation):</strong>
            <br/>Given <code>t₁ - t₂ = 1</code>
            <br/><code>132/x - 132/(x + 11) = 1</code>
            <br/><code>132 [(x + 11 - x) / (x(x + 11))] = 1</code>
            <br/><code>132 × 11 / (x² + 11x) = 1 &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; x² + 11x - 1452 = 0</code>
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 4 (Solve by factorisation):</strong>
            <br/>We need two numbers with sum = 11 and product = -1452.
            <br/>Factors: <code>44 × (-33) = -1452</code> and <code>44 - 33 = 11</code>.
            <br/><code>x² + 44x - 33x - 1452 = 0</code>
            <br/><code>x(x + 44) - 33(x + 44) = 0</code>
            <br/><code>(x - 33)(x + 44) = 0 &nbsp;⟹&nbsp; x = 33 &nbsp;or&nbsp; x = -44</code>.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Step 5 (Physical rejection &amp; conclusion):</strong>
            <br/>Since speed cannot be negative, we reject <code>x = -44</code>.
            <br/>Therefore, <code>x = 33 km/h</code>.
            <br/>Speed of passenger train = <strong>33 km/h</strong>.
            <br/>Speed of express train = 33 + 11 = <strong>44 km/h</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Interactive 20-Question Quiz -->
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Interactive CBSE Board Exam Quiz (20 Questions)</h2>
      <p class="muted">Test your command over factorisation, discriminant analysis, nature of roots, and quadratic word problems.</p>

      <div class="quiz-container card" id="quiz-box">
        <div class="quiz-header-bar">
          <span class="quiz-counter" id="quiz-counter">Question 1 of 20</span>
          <span class="quiz-score" id="quiz-score">Score: 0 / 20</span>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-question-body">
          <p class="quiz-q-text" id="quiz-question">Loading question...</p>
          <div class="quiz-options-list" id="quiz-options"></div>
          <div class="quiz-feedback" id="quiz-feedback"></div>
        </div>

        <div class="quiz-footer-actions">
          <button class="button secondary" id="quiz-prev-btn" disabled>← Previous</button>
          <button class="button" id="quiz-next-btn" disabled>Next Question →</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="quiz-completed-banner card" id="quiz-result-box" style="display:none; text-align:center; padding:2.5rem;">
        <h3>Quiz Completed! 🎉</h3>
        <p class="quiz-final-score" id="quiz-final-score" style="font-size:1.4rem; font-weight:700; color:var(--brand); margin:1rem 0;"></p>
        <p id="quiz-final-msg" class="muted"></p>
        <button class="button" id="quiz-restart-btn" style="margin-top:1rem;">Retake Quiz</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CTA -->
    <section class="cta-banner">
      <h2>Need personalized Maths guidance for Class 10?</h2>
      <p>Book a free {provider.trial.duration_minutes}-minute trial session with {provider.tutor_name} (online or at-home) to master quadratic equations and numerical word problems.</p>
      <a class="button" href={calBookingUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book Free Trial</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script is:inline>
(function() {
  const quizData = [
    {
      q: "Which of the following is a quadratic equation?",
      options: ["x² + 2x + 1 = (4 - x)² + 3", "-2x² = (5 - x)(2x - 2/5)", "(k + 1)x² + 3/2 x = 7 (where k = -1)", "x³ - x² = (x - 1)³"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "Expanding (x - 1)³: x³ - x² = x³ - 3x² + 3x - 1 ⟹ 2x² - 3x + 1 = 0, which is of degree 2 (quadratic). In option A, x² cancels on both sides."
    },
    {
      q: "The discriminant of the quadratic equation 2x² - 4x + 3 = 0 is:",
      options: ["-8", "8", "-16", "16"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "D = b² - 4ac = (-4)² - 4(2)(3) = 16 - 24 = -8."
    },
    {
      q: "If the equation x² + 4x + k = 0 has real and equal roots, then:",
      options: ["k < 4", "k > 4", "k = 4", "k ≥ 4"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "For real and equal roots, D = 0 ⟹ b² - 4ac = 0 ⟹ (4)² - 4(1)(k) = 0 ⟹ 16 - 4k = 0 ⟹ k = 4."
    },
    {
      q: "Values of k for which the quadratic equation 2x² - kx + k = 0 has equal roots are:",
      options: ["0 only", "4", "8 only", "0, 8"],
      answer: 3,
      explanation: "D = (-k)² - 4(2)(k) = 0 ⟹ k² - 8k = 0 ⟹ k(k - 8) = 0 ⟹ k = 0 or k = 8."
    },
    {
      q: "The roots of 100x² - 20x + 1 = 0 are:",
      options: ["1/10, 1/10", "-1/10, -1/10", "1/10, -1/10", "10, 10"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "(10x - 1)² = 0 ⟹ 10x - 1 = 0 ⟹ x = 1/10, 1/10."
    },
    {
      q: "If one root of the quadratic equation 2x² + kx - 6 = 0 is 2, then the value of k is:",
      options: ["1", "-1", "2", "-2"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Substitute x = 2: 2(2)² + k(2) - 6 = 0 ⟹ 8 + 2k - 6 = 0 ⟹ 2 + 2k = 0 ⟹ k = -1."
    },
    {
      q: "The quadratic equation 2x² - √5 x + 1 = 0 has:",
      options: ["Two distinct real roots", "Two equal real roots", "No real roots", "More than two real roots"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "D = b² - 4ac = (-√5)² - 4(2)(1) = 5 - 8 = -3. Since D < 0, it has no real roots."
    },
    {
      q: "If the sum of the roots of a quadratic equation is 6 and product is 9, the equation is:",
      options: ["x² - 6x + 9 = 0", "x² + 6x + 9 = 0", "x² - 9x + 6 = 0", "x² - 6x - 9 = 0"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "The equation is x² - (sum)x + product = 0 ⟹ x² - 6x + 9 = 0."
    },
    {
      q: "A natural number, when increased by 12, equals 160 times its reciprocal. Find the number:",
      options: ["8", "10", "12", "16"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "x + 12 = 160 / x ⟹ x² + 12x - 160 = 0 ⟹ (x + 20)(x - 8) = 0. Since x is a natural number, x = 8."
    },
    {
      q: "Which of the following equations has 2 as a root?",
      options: ["x² - 4x + 5 = 0", "x² + 3x - 12 = 0", "2x² - 7x + 6 = 0", "3x² - 6x - 2 = 0"],
      answer: 2,
      explanation: "For 2x² - 7x + 6 = 0: 2(2)² - 7(2) + 6 = 8 - 14 + 6 = 0. Hence, 2 is a root."
    },
    {
      q: "If 1/2 is a root of the equation x² + kx - 5/4 = 0, then the value of k is:",
      options: ["2", "-2", "1/4", "1/2"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "(1/2)² + k(1/2) - 5/4 = 0 ⟹ 1/4 + k/2 - 5/4 = 0 ⟹ k/2 - 1 = 0 ⟹ k/2 = 1 ⟹ k = 2."
    },
    {
      q: "The altitude of a right triangle is 7 cm less than its base. If hypotenuse is 13 cm, find the base:",
      options: ["5 cm", "12 cm", "9 cm", "10 cm"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Let base = x, altitude = x - 7. By Pythagoras theorem: x² + (x - 7)² = 13² ⟹ x² + x² - 14x + 49 = 169 ⟹ 2x² - 14x - 120 = 0 ⟹ x² - 7x - 60 = 0 ⟹ (x - 12)(x + 5) = 0. Base = 12 cm."
    },
    {
      q: "If the discriminant of ax² + bx + c = 0 is greater than zero and a perfect square, the roots are:",
      options: ["Real, rational and unequal", "Real, irrational and unequal", "Real and equal", "Non-real"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "When D > 0 and a perfect square (with rational coefficients), √D is rational. Hence the roots are real, rational, and unequal."
    },
    {
      q: "Two numbers differ by 3 and their product is 54. The numbers are:",
      options: ["6 and 9 (or -9 and -6)", "7 and 10", "5 and 8", "3 and 6"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "x(x + 3) = 54 ⟹ x² + 3x - 54 = 0 ⟹ (x + 9)(x - 6) = 0 ⟹ x = 6 or x = -9. Numbers are 6, 9 or -9, -6."
    },
    {
      q: "If the roots of px² + qx + 2 = 0 are reciprocal of each other, then:",
      options: ["p = 0", "p = 2", "p = -2", "q = 2"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "Product of roots = c/a = 2/p. Since roots are reciprocals, product = 1 ⟹ 2/p = 1 ⟹ p = 2."
    },
    {
      q: "The positive value of k for which both x² + kx + 64 = 0 and x² - 8x + k = 0 will have real roots is:",
      options: ["8", "16", "64", "4"],
      answer: 1,
      explanation: "For first equation: k² - 4(64) ≥ 0 ⟹ k² ≥ 256 ⟹ k ≥ 16. For second: (-8)² - 4k ≥ 0 ⟹ 64 ≥ 4k ⟹ k ≤ 16. Combining both: k = 16."
    },
    {
      q: "Solve for x: √3 x² + 10x + 7√3 = 0:",
      options: ["-√3, -7/√3", "√3, 7/√3", "-√3, 7", "√3, -7"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Product = √3 × 7√3 = 21, Sum = 10. Splitting 10x into 3x + 7x: √3 x(x + √3) + 7(x + √3) = 0 ⟹ (√3 x + 7)(x + √3) = 0 ⟹ x = -√3 or x = -7/√3."
    },
    {
      q: "If the roots of (b - c)x² + (c - a)x + (a - b) = 0 are equal, then:",
      options: ["2b = a + c", "b = a + c", "2a = b + c", "2c = a + b"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Notice x = 1 satisfies the equation since (b - c) + (c - a) + (a - b) = 0. Since roots are equal, both roots must be 1. Product of roots = (a - b)/(b - c) = 1 ⟹ a - b = b - c ⟹ 2b = a + c (i.e., a, b, c are in AP)."
    },
    {
      q: "A cottage industry produces a certain number of pottery articles in a day. The production cost of each article was 3 more than twice the number of articles produced. If total cost was ₹90, number of articles produced was:",
      options: ["6", "10", "12", "15"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Let articles = x. Cost per article = 2x + 3. Total cost = x(2x + 3) = 90 ⟹ 2x² + 3x - 90 = 0 ⟹ 2x² + 15x - 12x - 90 = 0 ⟹ x(2x + 15) - 6(2x + 15) = 0 ⟹ (x - 6)(2x + 15) = 0 ⟹ x = 6."
    },
    {
      q: "If x = 1 is a common root of ax² + ax + 3 = 0 and x² + x + b = 0, then ab equals:",
      options: ["3", "-3", "6", "-6"],
      answer: 0,
      explanation: "Substitute x = 1 in first: a(1)² + a(1) + 3 = 0 ⟹ 2a = -3 ⟹ a = -3/2. Substitute x = 1 in second: 1² + 1 + b = 0 ⟹ b = -2. Therefore, ab = (-3/2) × (-2) = 3."
    }
  ];

  let currentIdx = 0;
  let userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);

  const qText = document.getElementById("quiz-question");
  const optionsBox = document.getElementById("quiz-options");
  const feedbackBox = document.getElementById("quiz-feedback");
  const counterBox = document.getElementById("quiz-counter");
  const scoreBox = document.getElementById("quiz-score");
  const prevBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-prev-btn");
  const nextBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-next-btn");
  const quizBox = document.getElementById("quiz-box");
  const resultBox = document.getElementById("quiz-result-box");
  const finalScore = document.getElementById("quiz-final-score");
  const finalMsg = document.getElementById("quiz-final-msg");
  const restartBtn = document.getElementById("quiz-restart-btn");

  function renderQuestion(idx) {
    const item = quizData[idx];
    counterBox.textContent = `Question ${idx + 1} of ${quizData.length}`;
    qText.textContent = item.q;
    optionsBox.innerHTML = "";
    feedbackBox.textContent = "";
    feedbackBox.className = "quiz-feedback";

    const selected = userAnswers[idx];

    item.options.forEach((optText, oIdx) => {
      const btn = document.createElement("button");
      btn.className = "quiz-opt-btn";
      btn.textContent = `${String.fromCharCode(65 + oIdx)}. ${optText}`;

      if (selected !== null) {
        btn.disabled = true;
        if (oIdx === item.answer) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-correct");
        } else if (oIdx === selected) {
          btn.classList.add("opt-wrong");
        }
      } else {
        btn.onclick = () => selectOption(oIdx);
      }

      optionsBox.appendChild(btn);
    });

    if (selected !== null) {
      if (selected === item.answer) {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✓ Correct! ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-correct");
      } else {
        feedbackBox.textContent = `✗ Incorrect. Correct answer is option ${String.fromCharCode(65 + item.answer)}. ${item.explanation}`;
        feedbackBox.classList.add("feedback-wrong");
      }
    }

    prevBtn.disabled = idx === 0;
    nextBtn.disabled = selected === null;
    nextBtn.textContent = idx === quizData.length - 1 ? "Finish Quiz →" : "Next Question →";
    updateScoreDisplay();
  }

  function selectOption(oIdx) {
    userAnswers[currentIdx] = oIdx;
    renderQuestion(currentIdx);
  }

  function updateScoreDisplay() {
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    scoreBox.textContent = `Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length}`;
  }

  prevBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx > 0) {
      currentIdx--;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    }
  };

  nextBtn.onclick = () => {
    if (currentIdx < quizData.length - 1) {
      currentIdx++;
      renderQuestion(currentIdx);
    } else {
      finishQuiz();
    }
  };

  function finishQuiz() {
    quizBox.style.display = "none";
    resultBox.style.display = "block";
    let score = 0;
    userAnswers.forEach((ans, i) => {
      if (ans === quizData[i].answer) score++;
    });
    finalScore.textContent = `Your Final Score: ${score} / ${quizData.length} (${Math.round((score / quizData.length) * 100)}%)`;
    if (score >= 18) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Exceptional performance! You have complete command over quadratic equations and word problem modeling.";
    } else if (score >= 14) {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Good score! Review discriminant inequality problems and root conditions to achieve full marks.";
    } else {
      finalMsg.textContent = "Revise the factorisation patterns and Sridharacharya formula above, then try again!";
    }
  }

  restartBtn.onclick = () => {
    userAnswers = new Array(quizData.length).fill(null);
    currentIdx = 0;
    resultBox.style.display = "none";
    quizBox.style.display = "block";
    renderQuestion(0);
  };

  renderQuestion(0);
})();
</script>

